---
import DocsIndexLayout from '../layouts/DocsIndexLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<DocsIndexLayout
  title="How to use the ML interview field guide"
  description="Short, optional reading routes through the mlmentorship books for technical foundations, large-model systems, and research interviews."
>
  <header class="head">
    <p class="kicker">Front matter</p>
    <h1>Read by book or follow one focused route.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The table of contents is the main path. Use one route below only when you need to cross several books for a specific goal.
    </p>
  </header>

  {SITE.features.prepTools && <aside class="workbook-note"><strong>Preparing for an active interview loop?</strong> The <a href="/prep/">Workbook</a> combines role, rounds, current evidence, and due practice in one place.</aside>}

  <section id="starter-route" class="starter-route" aria-labelledby="starter-route-heading">
    <header><p class="kicker">Start here</p><h2 id="starter-route-heading">Three lessons, then choose your depth.</h2><p>Use this 30-minute route to see how the field guide teaches. Close each lesson and explain the mechanism before moving on.</p></header>
    <ol>
      <li><span>01</span><div><h3><a href="/concepts/matrices-as-linear-maps/">See a mechanism</a></h3><p>Build spatial intuition for a matrix before touching the formula.</p><small>Read the visual, close it, and explain what changes shape.</small></div></li>
      <li><span>02</span><div><h3><a href="/concepts/flashattention/">See a systems trade-off</a></h3><p>Follow memory movement and tiling instead of memorizing a kernel name.</p><small>Explain the bottleneck and one condition that would change the design.</small></div></li>
      <li><span>03</span><div><h3><a href="/questions/defend-values-under-ethical-pressure/">Practice interview judgment</a></h3><p>Work through a real trade-off, then defend the decision under pushback.</p><small>Answer closed-book before reading the leveled response.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="starter-route-next">Ready for a real loop? <a href="/prep/readiness/">Build the personalized map →</a></p>
  </section>

  <nav class="path-index" aria-label="Reading paths">
    <ol>
      <li><a href="#building-deep-technical-foundations"><span>01</span>Build technical foundations</a></li>
      <li><a href="#large-model-systems"><span>02</span>Study large-model systems</a></li>
      <li><a href="#research-to-industry"><span>03</span>Move from research to industry</a></li>
      <li><a href="#engineering-leader-hiring-manager"><span>04</span>Calibrate a senior ML hire</a></li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <section class="path" id="building-deep-technical-foundations">
    <header><span>01</span><div><h2>Build deep technical foundations</h2><p>Use this for a compact pass through math, learning, and transformer basics.</p></div></header>
    <ol>
      <li>Linear algebra: <a href="/concepts/matrices-as-linear-maps/">linear maps</a>, <a href="/concepts/svd-and-pca/">SVD and PCA</a>, <a href="/concepts/eigenvalues-and-spectral-theorem/">eigenvalues</a>.</li>
      <li>Probability: <a href="/concepts/maximum-likelihood-estimation/">maximum likelihood</a>, <a href="/concepts/bayes-rule-and-posterior/">Bayes rule</a>, <a href="/concepts/kl-divergence/">KL divergence</a>.</li>
      <li>Deep learning: <a href="/concepts/backpropagation/">backpropagation</a>, <a href="/concepts/attention-mechanism/">attention</a>, <a href="/concepts/transformer-architecture/">transformers</a>.</li>
      <li>Evaluation: <a href="/concepts/hypothesis-testing-confidence-intervals/">hypothesis testing</a>, <a href="/concepts/reproducibility-fair-model-comparison/">fair comparison</a>, <a href="/concepts/evaluation-validity-benchmark-contamination/">evaluation validity</a>.</li>
      <li>Use the <a href="/concepts/">concept index</a> only when an attempt exposes another gap.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="path" id="large-model-systems">
    <header><span>02</span><div><h2>Study large-model systems</h2><p>Use this for training, inference, accelerator, or Research Engineer loops.</p></div></header>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/concepts/transformer-compute-memory-accounting/">Count parameters, FLOPs, and memory</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/concepts/sharded-matrix-multiplication/">Derive communication from sharded tensor axes</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/concepts/accelerator-network-topology/">Map the layout to the accelerator network</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/concepts/strong-scaling-and-parallelism-selection/">Choose a parallel plan and measure MFU</a>.</li>
      <li>Attempt the worked <a href="/questions/plan-70b-training-run/">70B training plan</a>, then read <a href="/concepts/profiling-distributed-ml-workloads/">distributed profiling</a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="path" id="research-to-industry">
    <header><span>03</span><div><h2>Move from research to industry</h2><p>Use this when strong research experience must become clear interview evidence.</p></div></header>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/guides/as-vs-mle-vs-re/">Compare applied, engineering, and research role expectations</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/questions/critique-ml-paper/">Practice fair paper critique</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/questions/design-ablation-study/">Design a discriminating ablation</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/questions/most-ambitious-project/">Prepare the ambitious-project discussion</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/questions/present-technical-ml-project/">Present one project under interruption and pushback</a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="path" id="engineering-leader-hiring-manager">
    <header><span>04</span><div><h2>Calibrate a senior ML hire</h2><p>Use this to define the role and evaluate evidence at the intended level.</p></div></header>
    <ol>
      <li><a href="/guides/as-vs-mle-vs-re/">Define the role before writing the loop</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/guides/five-things-as-interview-tests/">Choose the capabilities the loop should test</a>.</li>
      <li><a href="/guides/l5-vs-l6-faang-ml/">Calibrate senior through senior-principal evidence</a>.</li>
      <li>Choose representative prompts from the <a href="/questions/">question index</a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/#curriculum">← Back to the full library</a></p>
</DocsIndexLayout>

<style>
  .head { max-width: 42rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; padding-bottom: 1.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-rule); }
  .kicker { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; color: var(--c-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .head h1 { margin: 0 0 0.7rem; font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.45rem); }
  .lede { margin: 0; color: var(--c-text-soft); font-family: var(--font-reading); font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  .workbook-note { margin: 0 0 2rem; padding: .8rem 0 .8rem .9rem; border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent); background: var(--c-bg-tint); color: var(--c-text-soft); font-family: var(--font-reading); font-size: .9rem; }
  .starter-route { margin: 0 0 3rem; padding: 1rem; border: 2px solid var(--c-text); background: var(--c-surface); scroll-margin-top: var(--sticky-offset); }
  .starter-route header { max-width: 38rem; padding-bottom: .8rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-rule); }
  .starter-route header .kicker { margin-bottom: .45rem; }
  .starter-route header h2 { margin: 0 0 .35rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .starter-route header p:last-child { margin: 0; color: var(--c-text-soft); font-family: var(--font-reading); line-height: 1.5; }
  .starter-route ol { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: .7rem; margin: 1rem 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .starter-route li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.4rem 1fr; gap: .55rem; margin: 0; padding: .7rem 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--c-rule); }
  .starter-route li > span { color: var(--c-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .7rem; }
  .starter-route h3 { margin: 0 0 .25rem; font-size: .92rem; }
  .starter-route h3 a { color: var(--c-text); text-decoration: none; }
  .starter-route h3 a:hover { color: var(--c-accent); text-decoration: underline; }
  .starter-route li p, .starter-route li small { display: block; margin: 0; color: var(--c-text-soft); font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .starter-route li small { margin-top: .35rem; color: var(--c-muted); font-size: .7rem; }
  .starter-route-next { margin: 1rem 0 0; padding-top: .7rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--c-rule); color: var(--c-text-soft); font-size: .82rem; }
  .starter-route-next a { color: var(--c-accent); font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .starter-route-next a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  .path-index { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .path-index ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--c-rule); }
  .path-index li { margin: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-rule); }
  .path-index a { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; gap: 0.7rem; padding: 0.72rem 0; color: var(--c-text); text-decoration: none; }
  .path-index a:hover { color: var(--c-accent); }
  .path-index span { color: var(--c-muted); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; }

  .path { margin-bottom: 3rem; scroll-margin-top: var(--sticky-offset); }
  .path > header { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 2rem 1fr; gap: 0.7rem; padding-bottom: 0.7rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-rule); }
  .path > header > span { padding-top: 0.2rem; color: var(--c-accent); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; }
  .path h2 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .path header p { margin: 0; color: var(--c-muted); font-family: var(--font-reading); font-size: 0.95rem; }
  .path ol { margin: 1rem 0 0 2rem; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-family: var(--font-reading); }
  .path li { margin: 0.55rem 0; color: var(--c-text-soft); line-height: 1.55; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--c-rule); font-size: 0.9rem; }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .path > header { grid-template-columns: 1.5rem 1fr; }
    .path ol { margin-left: 0.5rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .starter-route ol { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>